      "The region blends Jbala and Ghomara Amazigh traditions with the Andalusian heritage of the refugees of al-Andalus. Its most famous face is the blue-washed medina of Chefchaouen, the Blue Pearl, while Tétouan keeps the sound of Andalusian music and a cuisine shaped by Granada. Sufi zawiyas, the moussems of henna and harvest, the Gnawa and Issawa brotherhoods and the jellabas and burnouses woven in the Rif give the region a culture of strong identity, where Spanish is still widely understood along the coast.",
